{"ascii": "Christopher Inacio", "ascii_short": null, "biography": "Chris is the Chief Engineer of the CERT at Carnegie Mellon University.  He has 30 years of experience in industry and has previously worked at Texas Instruments, Spinnaker Networks (acquired by NetApp), Compunetix, as well as other parts of Carnegie Mellon University.  He has a Computer Engineering degree from Virginia Tech as well as additional graduate work focused on superscalar microprocessor design and embedded reliability at CMU.  He has worked professionally across the entire computing stack from robotics, FPGA accelerators for networking, real-time operating systems, networking and network analysis, compilers and tools, and computer security.  Outside of work he spends time with his wife and family, too much tinkering, and playing football (aka soccer).", "id": 113536, "name": "Christopher Inacio", "name_from_draft": "Christopher Inacio", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/inacio-Mar26.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/inacio-Mar26_MPhrPhy.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "[]", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/113536/", "time": "2012-03-26T09:52:08Z", "user": ""}